# Media upload & delete

Two storage APIs exist. Pick the right one before wiring UI.

## Which API?

| Use case | Front-end | Back-end | Store in DB |
|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|
| Entity image (avatar, product, service/space gallery path) | `fileUploadService` + `FileUpload` | `POST/DELETE /api/uploads/*` | Relative **`filePath`** (e.g. `companies/{id}/services/{id}/gallery/foo.jpg`) |
| Company web media library (folders, bulk, website assets) | `companyWebMediaService` | `/api/company-web-media/*` | Relative path under `companies/{id}/web/media/` |
| Pick existing library image (WebpageEditor, forms) | `SelectMediaDialog` | list + upload via company web media | Same relative path; display with `getMediaFileUrl` |

Do **not** mix APIs for the same folder. Media library files live under `companies/{companyId}/web/media`; entity uploads use domain-specific paths (see skill).

## `FileUpload` (`@/components/ui/file-upload`)

- **Single image**, crop dialog, client compression (>2 MB), progress bar.
- Props: `folderPath` (required), `onFileUploaded(filePath, fileUrl)`, optional `onFileDeleted`, `currentImagePath` / `currentImageUrl`, `maxSize` (MB, default 5), `cropAspectPresets`.
- On upload success: persist **`filePath`** on the entity — not the full URL.
- Inline delete (X on preview): calls `fileUploadService.deleteFile(currentImagePath)` when path is not an `http` URL.

## `companyWebMediaService` (`@/features/website/services/companyWebMedia`)

- `list`, `createFolder`, `upload(companyId, folderPath, files[])`, `delete(companyId, itemPath, type)`.
- Multi-file upload (no crop): `MediaUploadDialog` or direct `upload()`.
- Single image with crop in library: `FileUpload` with `folderPath={`companies/${companyId}/web/media${subPath}`}`.
- **Delete file/folder:** confirm first (`DeleteConfirmationDialog` or destructive `CustomDialog` footer); then `delete(..., 'file' | 'folder')` and refresh list.

## Display URLs

| Stored value | Helper |
|--------------|--------|
| General upload path | `formatAvatarUrl(filePath)` from `@/shared/utils` |
| Web media library path | `getMediaFileUrl(companyId, filePath)` |

Static files are served at `/uploads/...` (see `server.js`).

## Delete semantics (important)

| Pattern | Disk delete? | Entity update? |
|---------|--------------|----------------|
| `FileUpload` X button (has `currentImagePath`) | Yes — `/api/uploads/delete/:filePath` | Parent `onFileDeleted` should clear DB field |
| Gallery grid remove (`ServiceGalleryTab`, `SpaceGalleryTab`) | **No** — only removes path from entity array | Yes |
| Media library delete | Yes — `companyWebMediaService.delete` | N/A |
| Replace image via new upload | Old file may remain orphaned unless you explicitly delete | Yes — save new path |

When removing a **single** entity image (avatar, cover), delete the file **and** clear the DB field. Gallery “remove from gallery” currently unlinks only — document if orphan cleanup is required.

## Folder path conventions

```
companies/{companyId}/web/media[/{subPath}]   # media library
companies/{companyId}/services/{serviceId}/gallery
companies/{companyId}/spaces/{spaceId}/gallery
users/{userId}/profile
products                                        # system catalog
system/services
```

Match sibling features; include `companyId` when the entity is company-scoped.

## Back-end limits & auth

| Route | Auth | Limits |
|-------|------|--------|
| `/api/uploads/upload` | `authenticateToken` | Images only, **5 MB**, field `file` |
| `/api/company-web-media/upload` | `manage_company` | **20 MB**, up to **20** files, field `files` |
| Deletes | Same as parent route | Path traversal blocked in company web media (`sanitizeRelativePath`) |

New upload routes: follow [backend-api-routes.mdc](backend-api-routes.mdc); register in `server.js`.

## UI conventions

- Upload triggers: `Button variant="accent"` with `Upload` icon; progress via `ProgressBar variant="upload"`.
- Delete controls: [delete-destructive-actions.mdc](delete-destructive-actions.mdc) — `variant="destructive"` or OKLCH red for icon buttons.
- Destructive confirms: `DeleteConfirmationDialog` or `CustomDialog` + `variant="destructive"` Delete in footer.
- Feedback: `toast.success` / `toast.error`; refresh list or parent state after upload/delete.

